  // 
  // `riskLevel` is required; a call without it is rejected.
  // LOW: Commands that are strictly read-only, have no meaningful side effects, and have no credible disclosure or security impact. Examples: ls, cat, git status, git diff, SELECT-only queries, authenticated reads that only observe state.
  // MEDIUM: Commands with bounded, understood effects that are straightforward to reverse or reproduce and do not present a credible risk of severe harm. Examples: writing files outside system directories, npm install, git commit, git push, gh pr create, builds and test runs, scoped deletion of generated or agent-created files.
