  // Resolves for any exit code with `output` and `exitCode`. Emit `text(r)` for an exit-code header, other result fields, then raw output. Filter, slice, or count `output` in JavaScript first when its size is unknown, keeping the exit code and other result fields in what you emit. When output may be large, redirect it to a file in the same command (`cmd > <file> 2>&1`) and Read or search that file in the same Script; do not pipe it into `head`, `tail`, or `grep`, which hides the command's exit code. Commands are killed at `timeout`; raise it for long builds and test suites. Set `timeout` to about twice the expected duration, not a blanket maximum; for suites that may hang, prefer per-case time limits and progress output over one long timeout. A timeout resolves with `exitCode: null`, `signal: 'TIMEOUT'`, and the output captured before the kill. Output too large to return resolves without `output`, with `outputBytes` and `outputFile`, the kept log to Read in slices.
